rota lap 4668, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; hand-advanced past row 3 (N mod 5) because every row was read today and row 4 stood fewest at 12 against row 0's 20. Read the threshold, the-marked-value, TWO_ROOMS and the-clock-and-the-mark. The row's sense pointed straight at the lap: an exit code is a mark worn on a value at a seam, taken in at the door before any reasoning begins -- and the-marked-value's wreck rule covers an UNKNOWN mark while saying nothing about a known one that means two things.
think Reds first -- the cold roster read no red of mine; the standing dated_path (%626) is another lane's. Walked my lane's open rows: %532's fourth kind is a language custody ruling, %460's capability field is a design act, and neither is agent-doable.
think Followed the digraph twin family first -- three enumerations of the lexer's head table, and all three derive or are held byte-for-byte. Clean. Recorded as a negative reading rather than a lap.
think Then read what glow_desk_run_scan.sh says about glow_run: "glow_run draws the line itself, in its own contract rather than in its prose." True, and the prose it pointed at lived in the READER. Probed the binary: exit 1 meant both a failed lowering and a source never read; exit 2 meant both a declined file and a usage slip.
think FileNotFound, IsDir and StreamTooLong all returned through Zig's !u8 main, so downstream named them "lowering failed" -- a claim about a desk's content for bytes nobody had seen. That is the one that costs, and it is reachable three ways from a caller's own path argument.
obs Repair in glow/glow_run.rye: the read is caught rather than propagated, printing the error by name and returning a new 3 unreadable; both usage refusals return 4 usage; the //! head carries the five-row table where the number is returned.
obs The downstream scan gains a sixth stage, unreadable. glow_run's 4 usage stays unclassified on purpose -- that scan always hands over a path, so a usage answer would be a fault in the scan itself, and inventing a stage for it would give that fault a name reading like a fact about a desk.
obs The new guard reads three things and gates each at zero: declared (the head table), returned (main's own return sites), probed (six shapes on metal). Gates rather than a ratchet, because a code with two meanings is a fault on the lap it arrives.
obs The derivation states its precondition and refuses: returned is read at or past the pub fn main line, sound because the three helpers above it return an optional slice, a usize and a slice. A bare integer return above main reads derivation_unsound.
obs The pen's stub spells the contract in shell, so a mutation of the stub is a mutation of the METAL answer -- the half a table-versus-source reading can never reach. Two metal_disagrees legs restore the exact elder collision and watch the guard refuse it.
obs An unbuilt binary reads verdict=unprobed with probes=0 rather than proven, keeping the source halves and naming the unread one -- %460's ruling one lane over.
